# Crusher-to-the-Bridge — AI Assistant Rules
#
# This file defines project conventions, data contracts, and architectural
# guardrails for AI code-generation assistants (Cursor, Copilot, Devin, etc.).

## Project Overview

Crusher-to-the-Bridge is a biodefense digital twin that simulates
multi-pathogen outbreaks on naval vessels.  It integrates:

- Agent-based modeling (Korkin Lab infection-dynamics engine)
- Four-pathway transmission core (direct, droplet, HVAC airborne, fomite)
- CONTAM-style multi-zone aerosol mass transport (py-contam bridge)
- GRUMB metagenomic surveillance (Dirichlet-multinomial CLR arrays)
- Instrument-level diagnostic simulation (6 modalities)
- Reactive Protocol Engine with cost-accounting ledger
- Multi-fidelity Artificial Lab Notebook (LOW/MID/HIGH)

## Repository Structure

```
orchestrator.py              — Main simulation loop (24 epochs)
dashboard.py                 — Streamlit multi-tab Tactical Command Deck
engines/
  infection_dynamics_bridge.py — Korkin Lab ABM adapter
  transmission_core.py       — Four-pathway dose model
  py_contam_bridge.py        — HVAC aerosol transport
crusher_labs/
  observation_core.py        — 6 diagnostic instruments + QC
  lab_notebook.py            — Three-tier fidelity serializer
  protocol_engine.py         — Stoplight-triggered SOP engine
  cost_ledger.py             — Financial/material/labor accounting
  modalities/                — Syndromic, PCR, RDT, sequencing
tools/
  sanity_checker.py          — Pydantic config validator
  gis_spatial_bridge.py      — GIS → JSON layout converter
data/
  config/
    protocols.json           — 7 standing operating protocols
    resource_costs.json      — Budget, inventory, per-test costs
    logging_profile.json     — Fidelity tier selection
  pathogens/
    active_profiles.json     — Multi-pathogen definitions
  platforms/destroyer_baseline/
    spatial_layout.json      — Zone nodes with display coords
    air_flow_paths.json      — HVAC zones, cross-zone links, adjacency
telemetry_buffer/
  simulation_history.json    — Per-epoch full state (24 records)
  artificial_lab_notebook.json — Instrument records (595+ per run)
schemas/                     — JSON Schema definitions for all data contracts
```

## Critical Data Contracts

### Pathogen Profile Keys (data/pathogens/active_profiles.json)
```
pathogen_id: str
name: str
category: str                     # "enteric_viral" | "respiratory_viral"
transmission_routes: list[str]    # subset of: direct_contact, fomite, droplet, hvac_airborne
shedding_curve_log10: list[float] # 15 entries (day-by-day)
asymptomatic_shedding_log10: list[float]
dose_adjustment: float
dose_response: {model: str, alpha: float, beta: float}
illness_probability: {eta: float, gamma: float}
recovery_day: int
surface_deposition_fraction: float  # must be in [0.0, 1.0]
base_susceptibility: float
microflora_disruption: {
  causes_disruption: bool,
  disruption_type: str,             # "gastrointestinal" | "respiratory"
  disruption_magnitude: float,
  affected_kingdoms: {Kingdom: {Taxon: float}}
}
introduction_epoch: int
initial_infected: int
```

### Spatial Zone Keys (data/platforms/*/spatial_layout.json)
```
id: str              # zone name (e.g. "Bridge", "MedBay")
type: str            # "Free" | "Dining" | "Room"
traffic: str         # "low" | "medium" | "high"
volume_m3: float     # must be positive
deck: str            # "upper" | "main" | "lower"
display: {x: float, y: float}
```

### Airflow Path Keys (data/platforms/*/air_flow_paths.json)
```
hvac_zones[]: {id: str, rooms: list[str], ach: float}
cross_zone_links[]: {from: str, to: str, flow_rate_m3h: float, is_hvac_ducted: bool, path: str}
adjacency[]: {from: str, to: str, type: str}
```
All zone/room references MUST exist in spatial_layout.json.

### Simulation History Per-Epoch Keys (telemetry_buffer/simulation_history.json)
```
epoch: int
trigger_status: str                          # "BASELINE" | "SUSPECTED" | "CONFIRMED"
agents: list[{agent_id, status, location, ...}]
spaces: {zone: {pathogen_mass, pathogen_mass_by_id, concentration_per_m3, volume_m3}}
summary: {susceptible, infected, isolated, recovered, immune, symptomatic, sick_call_count, disrupted_microflora_count, quarantine_refusers}
multi_pathogen: {pathogen_id: {infected, symptomatic, recovered, co_infected_count}}
contact_tracing: {epoch, shared_room_exposures, droplet_exposures, hvac_downstream_exposures, fomite_trailing_exposures, transmission_events}
reactive_protocols: {active_protocols, merged_modifiers, stoplights}
cost_accounting: {epoch, total_financial_usd, total_labor_hours, financial_balance_remaining, labor_hours_remaining, entries_count}
observation_engine: {air_sniffer, surface_swab, wastewater_sequencing, clinical_rdt, clinical_qpcr, clinical_microbiology, logging_fidelity}
microflora_shifts: {zone: {type, magnitude, delta_clr, ...}}
hvac: {transport_active, filter_type, filter_efficiency, ...}
crusher_ops: {surface_wipe_zones, pcr_results, rdt_positive_count, rdt_tested_count, isolated_agents}
```

### Lab Notebook Record Keys (telemetry_buffer/artificial_lab_notebook.json)
Common to all records:
```
sample_id: str                    # "CLN-{epoch}-{zone}-{assay}-{hash}"
timestamp_epoch: int
collection_point_type: str
collection_zone: str
assay_type: str                   # aerosol_pcr | surface_pcr | metagenomic_sequencing | lateral_flow_antigen | patient_qpcr | culture_and_staining | microflora_disruption_status | trigger_transition
fidelity_tier: str                # HIGH_FIDELITY | MID_FIDELITY | LOW_FIDELITY
binary_result: str                # "DETECTED" | "NOT DETECTED"
inferred_anomaly_score: float
qc_status: str                   # "QC_PASS" | "QC_FAILURE"
cross_contamination_carryover: float
```
HIGH_FIDELITY additions: raw_amplification_curve (list[40 floats]), background_fluorescence, kingdom_reads, kingdom_clr_deltas, read_counts, dirichlet_concentration

### Protocol Keys (data/config/protocols.json)
```
protocol_id: str                  # "SOP-001" through "SOP-007"
name: str
trigger: {instrument_class: str, stoplight_level: str, min_zones_affected: int}
modifiers: dict                   # keys vary by protocol type
costs_per_epoch: {financial_usd, materials: {item: count}, labor_person_hours}
activation_costs: {financial_usd, materials: {item: count}, labor_person_hours}
category: str                     # "intervention" | "surveillance"
```

## Modifier Scalar Constraints
These keys in protocol modifiers MUST be in [0.0, 1.0]:
- hvac_filter_efficiency_override
- surface_decontamination_factor
- surface_decay_rate_override
- ppe_transmission_reduction
- direct_contact_scalar
- droplet_scalar
- hvac_airborne_scalar

## Cross-Module Pipeline Flow
```
orchestrator.py
  ├─ infection_dynamics_bridge.py  →  agents, zone_pathogen_mass
  ├─ transmission_core.py         ←  agents, zone_pathogen_mass
  │                                →  ContactTracingMatrix, TransmissionEvents
  ├─ py_contam_bridge.py          ←  zone_pathogen_mass
  │                                →  updated_masses (HVAC transport)
  ├─ observation_core.py
  │   ├─ AirSniffer                ←  zone_airborne (60% of pathogen_mass)
  │   ├─ SurfaceSwab               ←  zone_surface  (40% of pathogen_mass)
  │   ├─ WastewaterSeq             ←  ww_pathogen_mass + microflora_shifts
  │   ├─ ClinicalRDT               ←  agent shedding_rate, symptom_status
  │   ├─ ClinicalQPCR              ←  agent specimen_mass
  │   └─ ClinicalMicrobiology      ←  agent microflora_disruption_status
  ├─ lab_notebook.py               ←  all instrument outputs
  │                                →  records[] in biosurveillance schema
  ├─ protocol_engine.py            ←  stoplights from observation_engine
  │                                →  active SOPs, physics modifiers
  └─ cost_ledger.py                ←  per-test + per-epoch costs
                                   →  FINANCIAL_AUDIT, running balances
```

## Coding Conventions

- Python 3.10+ with `from __future__ import annotations`
- Type hints on all function signatures
- Use `np.random.Generator` (not legacy `np.random.RandomState`)
- Constants at module top, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Classes use PascalCase; functions/methods use snake_case
- All file paths use `os.path.join()` for cross-platform support
- JSON files use UTF-8 encoding with 2-space indent
- Never hardcode zone names — always read from spatial_layout.json
- Never hardcode pathogen IDs — always iterate pathogen_profiles
- Probabilities and scalar modifiers must be validated in [0.0, 1.0]
- Room volumes, budgets, and ACH values must be non-negative
- Run `python tools/sanity_checker.py` before committing config changes

## Testing

```bash
# Generate simulation data (24-epoch run)
python orchestrator.py

# Validate configuration files
python tools/sanity_checker.py

# Launch dashboard
streamlit run dashboard.py

# Run from any directory (Windows)
run_dashboard.bat
```

## Sibling Repositories

These repositories provide mathematical foundations but are NOT modified
by this project:

- `infection-dynamics` — Korkin Lab Java ABM (MASON/GeoMason)
- `py-contam` — CONTAM I/O library for indoor air quality modeling
- `GRUMB` — Maritime microbiome bioinformatics pipeline
- `EMOD-Generic` — Epidemiological MODeling framework
- `FRED` — Agent scheduling and compliance framework
